title: The Hunger Chancellor
subtitle: Popular discontent with Chancellor [+ chancellor +] rises.
new-page: true
view-if: year >= 1931 and month >= 2 and disfavored >= 18 and welfare < 0 and works_program == 0
on-arrival: commons_marcher *= 0.9 if chancellor_party == "Marcher"; commons_marcher *= 0.9 if marcher_in_government == 1; commons_royalist += 5 if marcher_in_government; commons_collectivist += 4 if marcher_in_government; disfavored_royalist += 5 if marcher_in_government; dufour_angry += 10; dufour_angry_bruning += 10
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/Kollwitz_Hospital.jpg

= The Hunger Chancellor

People are calling Chancellor [+ chancellor +] the Hunger Chancellor because of his perceived callousness in the face of the depression. [? if chancellor_party == "Marcher" : This is obviously a very bad sign for us. ?]

[? if marcher_toleration == 1 : As we are currently tolerating the [+ chancellor +] government, this could very well reflect badly on us. ?]

- @maintain_toleration: Maintain the current governing arrangement.
- @break_toleration: Break toleration; vote against this government.

@maintain_toleration
subtitle: It is necessary to preserve democracy.
view-if: marcher_toleration == 1
on-arrival: commons_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 2; disfavored_royalist += 2; commons_marcher -= 2; pro_republic -= 2; collectivist_relation -= 2; ddp_left += 0.5

Our policy of toleration continues.


@break_toleration
subtitle: This is likely to result in new elections.
view-if: marcher_toleration == 1
on-arrival: next_election_time = time+3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 1; lvp_right += 1

We have definitively broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
